    "72": "The triangle formed by the lines \\(x - y = 0\\), \\(x + 2y = 3\\) and \\(2x + y = 6\\) is a:",
    "74": "Let \\(f\\) be any function defined on \\(\\mathbb{R}\\) and let it satisfy the condition \\(|f(x)-f(y)|\\le \\left|(x-y)^{2}\\right|,\\ \\forall\\,(x,y)\\in\\mathbb{R}\\). If \\(f(0)=1\\), then:",
    "79": "Let \\(R=\\{(P,Q)\\mid P \\text{ and } Q \\text{ are at the same distance from the origin}\\}\\) be a relation, then the equivalence class of \\((1,-1)\\) is the set:"
  },
  "authoredSolutions": {
    "72": "The line \\(x-y=0\\) has slope \\(1\\); \\(x+2y=3\\) has slope \\(-\\frac{1}{2}\\); \\(2x+y=6\\) has slope \\(-2\\). The acute angle between the first and second satisfies \\(\\tan\\theta=\\left|\\frac{1-(-1/2)}{1+1\\cdot(-1/2)}\\right|=3\\), and between the first and third \\(\\tan\\theta=\\left|\\frac{1-(-2)}{1+1\\cdot(-2)}\\right|=3\\). Two equal angles make the triangle isosceles. Hence (C)."
  }
